I added the "Draft" frame, but I couldn't open `other.designos`, so I don't have its frame names.

Opening a file replaces the current document. The open document has unsaved changes, so the tool refused. Forcing it would have discarded the Draft frame, which you haven't approved. Saving first would have broken your instruction not to save yet.

You can choose one of these:
1. Discard the Draft frame and open `other.designos`.
2. Save the current document to a path you pick, then open `other.designos`.

I explained this in `answer.md`.
